    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d5b24680-fbff-5cfd-beb6-9a15259181e8" activityNameId="96d5b3aa-f3b3-52d8-b70f-49314dd98f53" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethanol, 95% in H2O, from grass, at fermentation plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethanol, 95% in H2O, from grass, at fermentation plant
The multioutput-process "grass, to fermentation" delivers the co-products Ethanol, 95% in H20, from grass",  "fibres from grass", and "proteins from grass". The allocation is based on economic criteria. The production of ethanol from grass is of no economical importance in the world.;
UUID: 4ab18659-5fcd-32ae-adc3-bd1de825de23
Fermentation of grass including materials, energy uses, infrastructure, and emissions.
Location: The inventory is modelled with data from a pilot plant in Switzerland.
Technology: Production of ethanol from grass with the Saccharification and Simultanous Fermentation process.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: The production of ethanol from grass in Switzerland was 15000 hl in 2000.
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Some data are derived from other or unknown plants or have been estimated.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4ab18659-5fcd-32ae-adc3-bd1de825de23.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
